Switch (deko3d): a Tint GLSL option to write gl_Position.z unchanged

Tint's GLSL writer remaps every vertex's z from WebGPU's [0, w] clip range to GL's [-w, w] with
2 * z - w (raise/shader_io.cc), which rounds z to about 2^-24 of w (bug B7: Outset's shore foam
decals flickered). The deko3d renderer creates its device with DkDeviceFlags_DepthZeroToOne, whose
clip space has WebGPU's z range, so its shaders must not remap. Options::depth_zero_to_one (default
false) skips the remap; switch/deko/shader_translate.cpp sets it.

The Tint half of the removed dawn-switch-gl-clip-control.patch (whose GL half set
glClipControl(GL_LOWER_LEFT, GL_ZERO_TO_ONE) in Dawn's GL backend), unchanged but for comments.

